{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he shall confess that wherein he has sinned.</b> That he set it to his heart and recalled the sin after it had been hidden from him and he was in doubt about it, and now returns to certainty — and this is the sense of והתודה, from the root of ודאי (certainty). And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted that this verse teaches that every sin-offering requires confession (viddui), and so they interpreted in the Sifre on the verse (Numbers 5:6) ״ואשמה הנפש ההיא״ — a paradigm for all the dead, that they require confession."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:57.178386434Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}